Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Bundles", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell["\<\
We start with a finite graph and a projection of its vertices. Equal fibers, \
lift existence, unique lifting and bundle structure are separate properties. \
Sections and complete connections add choices to this data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd5e75fb-ba3d-4d50-b7f2-02d7b3e1519c"],

Cell["Topological language and finite readings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"595b49a5-fc57-43be-a7a4-9368827bfe14"],

Cell["\<\
The finite object is a graph with a vertex projection. The following \
dictionary distinguishes its exact conditions from the additional structures \
of continuous topology.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b1fb8aa-2171-42bf-9ba9-356efe775247"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "554cabfd-6655-42e7-864c-b88b2ebfd5d6"], Cell[
    "Topological notion", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"7da1bf37-7a12-4be5-9f8d-fe363b95487b"],
     Cell["Finite infra reading", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"d55a4a22-569a-4a8a-915a-3fb2640228b5"],
     Cell["Qualification", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"7649f75d-c913-4616-b87f-9c39305e4624"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "a6d57606-be21-462a-9469-90e13b91f2e6"], Cell[
    "Projection from total space to base", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "81e1f4b0-a711-4b6f-9ea8-4efd15ba0e89"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberedGraph with InfraTotalSpace, InfraBaseSpace and InfraProjection\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4393ab61-78fa-4a92-abd8-1948bd95a6ae"], 
    Cell["\<\
The base graph is reconstructed from projected edges; no topology is part of \
the inert object.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"363f994c-9f00-47d8-9f63-b849ccc64445"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "825512e8-56fd-46f5-8f1b-1b965b916512"], Cell[
    "Serre or Hurewicz fibration", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "1b6f6de8-8c42-4447-8bab-8e8e457218c4"], Cell["\<\
InfraFibrationQ asks for a lift of every base edge from every starting vertex\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ccd06876-5605-4523-9114-615cd145fd6e"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is weak edge-lift existence, not a homotopy-lifting axiom.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"983a758e-8f72-4c69-92f5-cfd2a3f750dc"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "01548287-64d6-435f-a17b-25c515c2a150"], Cell[
    "Covering space", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e2c99c45-beb7-46ba-a830-4795616b6c52"], Cell["\<\
InfraCoveringQ gives edgeless fibers and a bijection on vertex neighbourhoods\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"73a02227-b625-4261-aeb4-d15ac13435f2"], 
    Cell["\<\
The graph-covering condition has the usual covering interpretation under \
graph realization. Sheet counts can differ across base components.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c434c213-4d8f-427f-8d13-78c9e603a2b6"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "6a6c91e3-2d55-4039-b365-f475a365583f"], Cell[
    "Fiber bundle", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "aa23d8be-f970-4d56-9719-1f36bf4a2fd6"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberBundleQ gives a common fiber graph and adjacency-preserving \
transverse matchings\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"924b8fd2-7332-4174-90b2-1bda2cd771f8"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is an edgewise Cartesian graph bundle. Realizing its edges alone does \
not supply topological product charts or filled squares.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"fccc0c1b-f8ee-4232-bb01-64c166ef6f7e"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "121b956e-7cae-4b3c-a802-0211f8b58b93"], Cell[
    "Section", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "652f9a2c-5653-4a37-8c76-af8cb8c3ebcf"], Cell[
    "InfraSection chooses a right inverse on a base domain", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"7dc8d572-f700-4621-8d97-f16f47b4c869"], Cell["\<\
InfraContinuousSectionQ asks for adjacency preservation on that domain.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6fc2760b-350b-4b63-a758-4e100c67090d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "fb065a5d-ab88-452f-b94f-73fb4561c6e8"], Cell[
    "Connection and parallel transport", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "726ba03a-9ed5-4d7a-9c78-255a83199ee0"], Cell["\<\
InfraConnection selects complete fiber matchings; transport composes them\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"26bf4447-403e-4f1e-8739-ba8e5aaf8e2b"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is finite bijective transport. Preserving a fiber graph is an additional \
condition.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"93fa2c1f-3411-478b-b4ae-f93a9e38b2e3"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "32ecf66a-d96f-4b30-8c40-7f58ebef780f"], Cell[
    "Infra-only transverse local conditions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "cdd6e6a1-e0b8-411d-8d1a-cf4a1e929307"], Cell["\<\
InfraAtMostOneEdgeLiftQ and InfraFibrationQ read injectivity and surjectivity \
on transverse neighbours\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"75117b08-3fe3-4f48-9f3c-240f6302a7c9"], 
    Cell["\<\
Vertical neighbours are excluded; the conditions do not assert local \
injectivity or surjectivity in a chosen topology.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b5cf942d-f155-4514-8b31-aa23dc7fff1a"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "ef5d8b0d-eff9-4577-ade5-425b3ffb5cea"], Cell[
    "Infra-only multiplicity and equitable partition", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"2bf904d6-8e31-45a6-94ff-785ef0e87ee8"], Cell["\<\
InfraEdgeLiftMultiplicity counts transverse neighbours, including zeros\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8a63b08f-f045-4b73-b35c-195f953c6811"], 
    Cell["\<\
Constancy within each fiber is transverse equitability; full equitability \
also needs constant vertical degree.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"3acc0cc1-32af-47ca-b162-73ebfbd65bcd"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"dcac80ef-bbaf-43d5-bc8e-\
16f57d7088f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the continuous definitions, see ",
 ButtonBox["Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Sections 1.3 and 4.2",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf"], None}],
 ". The finite definitions and their implications are developed below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a675c03-8d5e-4d6b-8d20-908152cdf13f"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"583c8cbc-c485-48ec-b6d8-59a1b5bbf88e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", " ", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`\>\"", " ", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7337c86d-8e36-4e3e-815f-2fe3873c6052"],

Cell["Total space, projection and fibers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9ff9a418-2a16-412f-a88a-e1183873153e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["fibered graph", "TI"],
 " consists of a finite simple undirected unweighted untagged graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fa386aaf-737e-481c-b53c-61c881a567ee"],
 " and a map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c1945e6-5143-493e-855e-6f0df6e72a95"],
 " on its vertices. The ",
 StyleBox["base graph", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7732f777-644f-4922-9506-cd66920840ae"],
 " has vertex set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d36b7e2-8f31-49ae-a34a-69c45f38a97d"],
 ". Distinct base vertices are adjacent exactly when some total edge joins \
their preimages. The ",
 StyleBox["fiber", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0601447c-543a-4531-a039-850ccae61b9a"],
 " is the induced graph on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eeefc2e0-e442-46ea-92f5-1da54fb7e8cf"],
 ". A total edge is ",
 StyleBox["vertical", "TI"],
 " when both endpoints project to the same vertex, and ",
 StyleBox["transverse", "TI"],
 " otherwise."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"94376401-a4f6-4f23-a366-f4dac3e1b61e"],

Cell["\<\
The object carries no drawing, connection or lifting axiom. The base includes \
isolated projection values, and projection collapses vertical edges. The \
empty graph with empty projection is allowed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8d329fb1-740e-4a94-bc1b-16c0cbd82732"],

