Cell["\<\
Section and connection samplers return one object by default. An integer \
result count requests exactly that many distinct objects, a capped count \
requests at most that many, and All enumerates the class. An exact shortage \
gives an empty result list. These result counts are distinct from the vertex \
and edge count specifications above.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aa5e4a30-0077-480f-b9e6-f84e2332ad33"],

Cell["\<\
The external random seed controls bounded random searches. Identity ordering \
and default complete enumeration are deterministic. A pruning callback \
restricts the searched class, so a shortage under that callback need not mean \
mathematical nonexistence.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4934f33-eaa2-4183-8e34-17e90fe97813"],

Cell["Complete connections and horizontal lifts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dab936cf-f478-409a-bda1-cd21d56c213c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["complete connection", "TI"],
 " selects a perfect matching between the whole fibers over every base edge, \
using transverse total edges. It selects no vertical edges. A matching \
transports fiber vertices bijectively, but need not preserve vertical \
adjacency."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63ff3552-bbcd-42da-a159-d9f23246353b"],

Cell["\<\
Lift existence alone does not supply a complete connection. In this example \
every total vertex has a transverse neighbour, but the first two vertices of \
one fiber share only one possible target. No perfect matching can use \
distinct targets for both.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d225438-3bc4-4129-ba04-83b8972f6178"],

